    This is more the direction I hope that future versions of hack take.
Most suggestions have dealt with new items or new character classes.  I'd
like to see whole new types of challenges/encounters that add depth to the
game, such as:

    A Ruins Level:  A huge cavern with several buildings, maybe an old 
             library, an old temple, etc.  Buildings could collapse if
             walls are damaged, staircase down could be hidden under
             rubble.  Ghosts, Wights, and Skeletons should abound.

    A Forest level:  Have trees which can be "climbed", which amounts to
             levitating, and then only traveling from "tree" to "tree".
             When you are "climbing" it should appear on the status line.
             Introduce rivers, perhaps with boats, (draw)bridges, etc.
             Whole area should be "dark", so as to be more spooky.  
             Monsters should drop on you from above.  Some stuff could
             be hidden in trees.  All sorts of monsters appropriate to 
             a forest could be used.

    A Town level:  Shops, Police department, Bar/delicatessen, Lots of 
             characters wandering around.  If you start a fight in a bar
             *everyone* fights, police show up, etc.

    Islands:  Have to navigate from one island to another.  There could
            be a current in the river (each move you make has a high
            chance of being altered in the direction of current flow).
            Put exit near downstream end.  (Assumes that swimming is
            introduced as new mode).

    An Ogre Castle:  Lots of nasty ogres, an Ogre King, maybe Ogre Magi
            (from D&D - they can shoot blasts of cold, and turn invisible.)
            Have to break in somehow and find treasure.

    Dark "Big Rooms":  Light spells should not work, so you have to 
            explore the whole thing.

    Watery Levels:  Need  waterwalking boots, leviation, or teleportation
            to cross (or spell, "part water").  You have to hunt around 
            on earlier levels to find what you need...

    Hidden Sublevels:  Have a secret stairway that leads to a level hidden
           between levels.  These are useful for all sorts of things:
           Department stores (multilevel shops), crossing caverns or 
           barriers, etc.

    Orc, Centaur, or other Humanoid Villages:  Again, lots of peaceful
           monsters, who will beat on you if you start a fight.  They might
           help you kill monsters, too, on that level (and then take the
           treasure, of course!).

    After all, there are ~25 levels of just mazes in the game.  I think some of
them could be made more interesting.  The town/village/ogre levels might
act differently when you have the amulet.  These special levels should not
be identical from game to game the way the castle currently is.

    Other random thoughts:

    Introduce "signposts" with messages on them, and trees.

    Have "fires", which flicker as your character moves: alternate
           ' and `  characters.  Have flaming walls, set chest on
           fire when wands or dragons flame them, etc.

    Make Kops MUCH more potent, as you rob more stores, and have them 
           reappear unexpectedly since you are now a wanted criminal.

    Have shopkeepers refuse admittance to anyone who has robbed a shop.

    Have police show up after a shopkeeper is killed (after a delay, or
           after the player has left the level and returned).  Or have
           grieving family members show up.  (How is that for guilt!)

           "My name is Inigo Asidonhopo" -more-
           "You killed my father" -more-
           "Prepare to die!"  

    Introduce grenades:  Throw them, and they explode in an area of 
           effect.

    Introduce Portals:  Point to point teleporters on a given level.

    Have three staircases down in a room.  Two lead to traps/single rooms
           full of monsters/teleport you to level 1/something else bizarre.

    Have intelligent monsters act intelligently:  Have them *use* the
           treasure they carry i.e. rings of invisibility, wands, etc.
           I think that Ring Wraiths never wear their rings.  Liches
           should be able to turn invisible.

    Introduce a Thief, who robs characters and *runs away*.  The thief
           should have a lair on some level.  He should move rapidly,
           and be hard to kill.  His lair should not have to be on the
           same level as the character.  He should steal things that 
           are valuable, not in a random fashion.

            "The thief hits! You are struck unconscious...-more-
             You wake to find that your Ring of Conflict is missing."
     

    Hide Stairways under rubble and stuff...

    Vampires should be nastier.  They should bite your neck and drain
           you of a fraction of your hitpoints.  They should also be 
           immune to anything but *blessed* weapons.  
          
           "You hit the vampire! -more-
            His wound closes immediately after you hit."    

    Polymorphed items should always be *less* valuable than the originals,
            to frustrate polypilers.

    There should be some monster that specializes in polymorphing the
            player, perhaps into a frog or something like that.

    I realize that some of these will be very hard to code.  I am just
trying to suggest much broader changes to the game than the "introduce
a +3 weed whacker" type of suggestion.  Are any of these possible?  Desired?
I especially like the thief idea.  He should only steal one or two items
(not as many as the nymph) but they should all be valuable.  

    In conclusion, I apologize if this is incoherent (it's 3:30am).  But
I think *some* of these ideas are implementable.


